From 9a05d83ef06514e8d3a4dbdaec2aa0ec35950f52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abayoumy <abayoumy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:28:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MQTT: stop exposing the auto-off timers to Home Assistant

The four `number` auto-off timers and their four `sensor` remaining-times were
indices 25..32 of the discovery table, and the device published `<base>/timerN`
and `<base>/timer_remainingN` state for them, so every reconnect re-announced 8
entities per strip (16 across both) that the owner does not want in HA.

The table now ends at the trip sensor (MTTL_HA_ENTITIES 34 -> 26,
MTTL_HA_TRIP_INDEX 33 -> 25; the trip entity keeps its topic), and both timer
state publications are gone together with the fields that fed them
(mqtt_timer_minutes, mqtt_remaining_*). Timers stay a device local feature: the
web UI, the buttons and the MQTT `.../timerN/set` command path are untouched, as
is the timer persistence path in sdk_worker.c.

The host test asserts the whole table: no `number` component anywhere, no `timer`
topic, and nothing at or past MTTL_HA_ENTITIES.
